# Physics workspace agent instructions

Read ../CLAUDE.md fully for the general integrity and supervision rules. Within
this workspace, use SCHEMA.md and WORKFLOW.md; tools/physics-autopilot owns all
transitions. Root mathematics tools and briefs are unchanged and are not physics
authoring instructions. Use this workspace as cwd and keep all authored content,
plans, tasks, evidence, and state here.

Never edit outside this workspace or change imported mathematical snapshots.
Read research/math-imports.json to identify imports. Mathematical prerequisites may use published/unpublished items or planned results
in root mathematics prose scaffolds, with exact statements, hypotheses, proof
status and consumer mappings. Develop remaining missing prerequisites locally
with domain: mathematics and purely mathematical dependencies. Source permission
does not certify a plan as proved or authorize original mathematical edits.
Never repair a published original mathematical supplier from a physics run.

Apply the class-specific requirements in SCHEMA.md at every authoring, reader,
refuter, adjudication, judgment, and repair stage. Thought experiments have exactly
the same proof obligations as physics theorems. Postulates and experiments need
source and scope review, not invented deductive proofs. Never invent measurements,
full-text retrieval, audits, or certainty. Carry empirical uncertainties and
physical applicability conditions into every consuming physical conclusion.

A physical item's declared scope and empirical qualifications form part of its
public claim. Postulate formulations and experiment setup, procedure, observations,
uncertainty, and interpretation are also public interfaces. Changes to them require
direct and indirect consumer review under the general statement-change rule. Verification stamps,
citations, and proof-only changes alone do not propagate. Mathematical items retain
the original Statement/Definition interface rule.

Before authoring, judging, or adjudicating statistical physical claims, read the
statistical-evidence and double-slit section of ../PHYSICS-CONTENT-MODEL.md.
Experiments support or constrain specified models; finite data do not prove a
framework. Review confidence is not certainty about nature.

## Required mathematical rigor and explicit definitions

This rule applies to all physics frameworks, not only general relativity.
Be as mathematically rigorous and explicit as possible. Read “Mathematical rigor
and explicit definitions” in ../PHYSICS-CONTENT-MODEL.md. Provide explicit
mathematical definitions before using technical physical terms, with the objects,
spaces, maps, regularity, hypotheses, and conventions specified. Define locally
or use an exact earlier supplier and make its relevant definition explicit; do
not substitute terminology or a textbook citation for a definition. Reuse
established definitions without unnecessary repetition.

In particular, define reference frames and worldlines using the differential
geometry appropriate to the framework: specify spacetime structure, curve domain,
regularity, parameter and causal conditions where applicable, and whether a frame
means an adapted chart, observer congruence, or basis/tetrad field. Do not conflate
these notions or import relativistic assumptions into a nonrelativistic model.
Scaffolders and authors must supply missing mathematics locally or flag the exact
open prerequisite. Reviewers, judges, and adjudicators must check these definitions
and reject concealed prerequisite gaps or deductions resting on undefined terms.
Preserve the distinction between mathematical precision and empirical certainty.

## Current six-step numbering

For outside Codex repair agents in this physics workflow, use medium effort for Steps 1–3 and 6 and high effort for Steps 4–5; this supersedes the older numerical mapping in ../CLAUDE.md for physics only. Engine-dispatched Step-2 scope reviewers and repairers use the owner-selected GPT-6 Luna max profile and follow their own briefs. Step 1 performs initial authoring, Step 2 reviews scope/prerequisites, Step 3 is independent review, Step 4 is batch review/judging, Step 5 adjudicates/repairs, and Step 6 closes out.

