      "statement": "Assume \\(\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega\\), and let \\(\\pi:P\\to M\\) be a smooth right principal \\(G\\)-bundle for a finite-dimensional real Lie group \\(G\\), with \\(\\mathfrak g=\\operatorname{Lie}(G)=T_eG\\). A supplied principal connection is a smooth, right-invariant complement \\(TP=VP\\oplus H\\), where \\(VP=\\ker d\\pi\\); write \\(v:TP\\to VP\\) for the projection along \\(H\\), and let \\(K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])\\) be its vertical-valued curvature. For \\(Z\\in\\mathfrak g\\) and \\(p\\in P\\), define the fundamental vertical vector \\(Z_P(p)=\\left.\\frac{d}{dt}\\right|_{t=0}p\\exp_G(tZ)\\). The orbit differential \\(\\zeta_p: \\mathfrak g\\to V_pP\\), \\(Z\\mapsto Z_P(p)\\), is a linear isomorphism, as proved below. Define the **principal connection 1-form** by\n\n$$\\omega_p(X):=\\zeta_p^{-1}(v_pX),\\qquad X\\in T_pP.$$\n\nThen \\(\\omega\\) is a smooth \\(\\mathfrak g\\)-valued 1-form satisfying \\(\\omega(Z_P)=Z\\), \\(\\ker\\omega=H\\), and \\(R_g^*\\omega=\\operatorname{Ad}_{g^{-1}}\\omega\\) for every fixed \\(g\\in G\\). Conversely, a smooth \\(\\mathfrak g\\)-valued 1-form with the reproduction and equivariance properties determines the principal connection \\(H=\\ker\\omega\\). The converted vertical curvature \\(\\kappa_H:=\\omega\\circ K_H\\) is a \\(\\mathfrak g\\)-valued alternating 2-form; its equality with the Cartan curvature is established in the curvature lemma.",
