## Definition

Let $n\geq1$, let $U\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be nonempty and open, let $\mathcal F_U$ be the finite-jet local algebra with nilpotent BRST derivation $s$ and commuting total derivatives $D_\mu$, and let $dx^1,\ldots,dx^n$ be anticommuting coordinate one-forms. For $g\in\mathbb Z$ and $0\leq p\leq n$, let $\mathcal A_U^{g,p}$ be the space of local horizontal $p$-forms of ghost number $g$, namely finite sums of $dx^{\mu_1}\wedge\cdots\wedge dx^{\mu_p}$ with coefficients in the ghost-number-$g$ part of $\mathcal F_U$. Define the horizontal differential $d_H:=dx^\mu D_\mu$; commuting $D_\mu$ and anticommuting $dx^\mu$ give $d_H^2=0$. Extend $s$ to horizontal forms by $s(dx^\mu\wedge a)=-dx^\mu\wedge sa$, so $sd_H+d_Hs=0$.

The local BRST cohomology modulo total derivatives in bidegree $(g,p)$ is

$$H^{g,p}(s\mid d_H):=\frac{\{a\in\mathcal A_U^{g,p}:\text{there is }b\in\mathcal A_U^{g+1,p-1}\text{ with }sa+d_Hb=0\}}{\{sm+d_Hn:m\in\mathcal A_U^{g-1,p},\ n\in\mathcal A_U^{g,p-1}\}}.$$

For $p=0$, set $\mathcal A_U^{g,-1}=\{0\}$. This is cohomology of the specified local jet algebra and horizontal differential; it is not cohomology of a physical state space or Hilbert space. Interpreting $d_H$-exact top forms as equal local functionals additionally assumes compact support or boundary conditions that make the corresponding surface term vanish.

