+### def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action — authored
+
+Claim/convention: field antifields have opposite parity and ghost number -1-gh(field); the canonical antibracket uses right derivatives on its first argument and left derivatives on its second, with ghost degree +1. The minimal candidate is the BRST-variation coupling to antifields plus a specified gauge-invariant local S0; it is called a master action only when it satisfies the CME. Optional antighost/Nakanishi–Lautrup variables are explicitly nonminimal, with s(bar c)=b and sb=0, but no cohomological contractibility claim is made. The infinite-dimensional functional notation is conditional and does not define a measure, BV Laplacian, path integral, or QME.
