+# Batch 4 authoring notes
+
+Run: advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23  
+Pair: qftx-nonabelian-brst-bv-mathematics and its examples companion.
+
+## Plan and dependency audit
+
+The assigned design at research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md, the current research/plan-spec.json pair, and the batch-4 manifest agree on the page IDs, order 960, title, category/library, A/B pairing, and qftx-gauge-geometry prerequisite. The active plan's two item arrays are empty; the design names five future A items and the owner direction treats empty B inventories as placeholders. This is an expected pre-authoring inventory difference, not a conflicting page interface. The A manifest now receives the five planned items; the B manifest receives two worked examples.
+
+The run's research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json places batch 4 at level 1, requiring batch 2. The item graph is separate from that page edge. Planned item dependencies are being made explicit where the mathematical structure requires them: the BRST nilpotence lemma depends on the finite-jet BRST definition; relative local cohomology also depends on the nilpotence lemma so its quotient is a cochain cohomology; BV data depend on the BRST field/sign conventions and nilpotence result; the BV master-equation lemma depends on the BV definition. No item in this pair will claim the missing global connection or curvature construction as an item-level result.
+
+The required provider page qftx-gauge-geometry is present. Its current A inventory lists def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data, def-qftx-principal-connection-form, def-qftx-lie-algebra-valued-form-bracket, lem-qftx-principal-curvature-cartan-bianchi, and def-qftx-associated-covariant-derivative. Their actual current carriers and complete definition/proof sections were inspected. The exact conventions include a smooth right principal bundle, a supplied right-invariant horizontal complement, Z_P(p)=d/dt|_0 p exp_G(tZ), omega(Z_P)=Z, R_g^*omega=Ad_(g^-1)omega, the shuffle-normalized bracket, F=dA+1/2[A wedge A], and A_j=Ad_(g_ij^-1)A_i+theta_L(g_ij). The connection/curvature chain carries only the declared AC_omega premise.
+
+The initial in-progress readiness query used loadStep1Record and step1Decision from tools/physics-support/frontier-snapshot.mjs and tools/physics-support/step1-decisions.mjs; all five provider items then returned closed:false, reason “Readiness record missing”. The existing def-qftx-nonabelian-gauge-data is a complete definition carrier; the other four carriers have complete current definitions/proofs. Their status:draft and verification.precheck:pending are not treated as proof defects or independent-approval failures. A later fresh readiness query after those complete carriers were read returned current ready records for all five; see the final readiness refresh below. No batch-2 supplier was edited or represented as independently approved.
+
+## Item progress
+
+### def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex — authored
+
+Claim/convention: on a nonempty open coordinate patch U subset R^n, take a finite-dimensional real Lie algebra and a parity-preserving Lie-algebra representation on a finite-dimensional graded complex vector space. The finite-jet algebra has smooth coefficients, commuting even gauge-field jets, graded matter jets, and exterior ghost jets. Use sA_mu=partial_mu c+[A_mu,c], sc=-1/2[c,c], s psi=-rho(c)psi, with a left odd derivation and s(D_I Phi)=D_I(s Phi). This definition is local and algebraic; it does not assert a global bundle or quantum theory. No antighost/Nakanishi–Lautrup pair is included.
+
+Dependencies: none; dependency_level 0. Sources/locators: Barnich–Brandt–Henneaux, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0002245, §§2.2–2.3 and 4.1–4.2; Gomis–París–Samuel, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9412228, §§3.2 and 5.2. Their sign orders differ; this carrier states its own convention explicitly. No source-fetch stamp or scoped validation has been run yet.
+
+Unresolved obligations: prove nilpotence on gauge, ghost, and matter generators and extend it to finite jets; then define local cohomology and BV data from the actual local interfaces. Next: author lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence.
+
+### lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence — authored
+
+Claim/convention: for the exact finite-jet algebra and left-derivation convention in def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex, the ghost, gauge, and arbitrary-parity matter generators are square-zero; the operator commutes with each total derivative and its square extends as zero to every finite polynomial. The proof uses only the ordinary Lie-algebra Jacobi identity and the explicitly assumed representation identity.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex (mathematical-premise); dependency_level 1. Proof route: ghost bracket/Jacobi, gauge derivative cancellation plus Jacobi, matter representation identity, then total-jet extension. Sources/locators: Barnich–Brandt–Henneaux, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0002245, §§2.2–2.3 and 4.1; Gomis–París–Samuel, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9412228, §§3.2 and 5.2. No source-fetch stamp or scoped validation has been run yet.
+
+Unresolved obligations: local relative cohomology must depend on this square-zero result; BV data must retain the same field and sign convention. Next: author def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology.
+
+### def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology — authored
+
+Claim/convention: local horizontal p-forms are finite-jet coefficients times exterior coordinate forms; d_H=dx^mu D_mu, and s acts on forms with the sign that makes s d_H + d_H s=0. H^{g,p}(s|d_H) uses cocycles sa+d_Hb=0 modulo sm+d_Hn, with b of ghost number g+1/form degree p-1. The definition explicitly distinguishes this local algebraic cohomology from physical state-space cohomology and states the boundary condition needed only for the local-functional interpretation.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex and lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence, both mathematical-premise; dependency_level 2. Sources/locators: Barnich–Brandt–Henneaux, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0002245, §§2.3 and 4.1–4.5; Gomis–París–Samuel, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9412228, §§4.6 and 8.1. The local quotient is defined directly; no classification theorem is imported. No source-fetch stamp or scoped validation has been run yet.
+
+Unresolved obligations: specify the canonical BV field/antifield algebra, grading, bracket signs, center condition, and master-action candidate; prove the master-equation/nilpotence equivalence. Next: author def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action.
+
+### def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action — authored
+
+Claim/convention: field antifields have opposite parity and ghost number -1-gh(field); the canonical antibracket uses right derivatives on its first argument and left derivatives on its second, with ghost degree +1. The minimal candidate is the BRST-variation coupling to antifields plus a specified gauge-invariant local S0; it is called a master action only when it satisfies the CME. Optional antighost/Nakanishi–Lautrup variables are explicitly nonminimal, with s(bar c)=b and sb=0, but no cohomological contractibility claim is made. The infinite-dimensional functional notation is conditional and does not define a measure, BV Laplacian, path integral, or QME.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex and lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence, both mathematical-premise; dependency_level 2. Sources/locators: Gomis–París–Samuel, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9412228, §§4.1–4.6 and 5.2; Qiu–Zabzine, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.2680, §§3.1–3.2 and 4.1–4.4. The latter is a finite-dimensional lecture-note treatment; its explicit warning about undefined infinite-dimensional operations is retained.
+
+Unresolved obligations: prove the exact iff between the CME and nilpotence of the Hamiltonian differential under the stated center condition; finish both companion examples. Next: author lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence.
+
+### lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence — authored
+
+Claim/convention: for the degree-one odd canonical antibracket and even ghost-number-zero S_BV, the left Hamiltonian differential sF=(S_BV,F) is square-zero exactly when (S_BV,S_BV)=0, provided the domain has no nonzero ghost-number-one central element. The proof derives s-squared from shifted Jacobi, then proves both directions; the converse center hypothesis is explicit rather than inferred from Jacobi alone. The finite-dimensional polynomial coordinate algebra satisfies it; any formal local-functional extension must verify it separately.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action (mathematical-premise); dependency_level 3. Sources/locators: Gomis–París–Samuel, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9412228, §§4.2–4.3 and 4.6; Qiu–Zabzine, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1105.2680, §§4.2–4.4. Gomis uses the opposite Hamiltonian ordering in its displayed BRST derivation; the local item fixes s=(S_BV,-) and derives the corresponding sign directly.
+
+Unresolved obligations: finish the finite SU(2) BRST and BV ghost-sector examples, create exact proof contracts, coverage/source stamps, cross-batch evidence, and item readiness dispositions. Next: author the two B-page examples.
+
+### ex-qftx-su2-brst-nilpotence — authored
+
+Claim/convention: in the fundamental SU(2) representation with anti-Hermitian generators T_a=-i sigma_a/2, the component BRST formulas are the specialization of the A-page convention and the nilpotence lemma. The verification checks the Pauli-matrix commutator and applies the general lemma; it does not claim a global connection or physical result.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex and lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence; dependency_level 2. No external source is claimed for the generated example; its exact suppliers are linked in Example references.
+
+### ex-qftx-su2-bv-ghost-master-equation — authored
+
+Claim/convention: the finite ghost/ghost-antifield algebra for su(2) has the canonical degree-one antibracket and S_CE=(1/2)c* epsilon c c; direct component contraction reduces its CME to the su(2) Jacobi identity. The example is limited to this finite algebraic sector, not a full Yang–Mills model.
+
+Dependencies: def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action and lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence; dependency_level 4. No external source is claimed for the generated example; its exact suppliers are linked in Example references.
